{
  "additional_concerns": [
    "All 12 required pairs are retained. NOT_APPLICABLE findings concern the typed gift questions; they neither authorize pruning the separate duties nor establish overall candidate correctness.",
    "Scope placement changes executable answers. With distributor status true and offering false, node.142f34016b300f5c110eb249 and node.bc55be7e973a689d07f9e64b can return FALSE, whereas node.2a6321b4ce90763bf0be564e returns OUT_OF_SCOPE. Promotional scope similarly affects other candidates. The intended distinction between a negative answer and OUT_OF_SCOPE remains unresolved.",
    "Unknown scope can block a determinate answer despite a known discount or non-gift classification. The circular does not prescribe this uncertainty policy or the global conflict-blocking policy.",
    "The offer-level candidates combine offer-level promotion with an existential gift component. Unless the supplied classification connects the same gift component to the qualifying promotion, unrelated components could jointly produce an unsupported prohibition.",
    "The circular defines distributors as intermediaries distributing SFC-authorised funds, while paragraph 10 uses broader investment-product language. Preserve both contextual actor scope and the quoted product wording; equivalence of the candidates' differing definitions is not established.",
    "Guaranteed returns and incentives are only potentially gifts. Neither structured-product status nor its absence settles gift classification. The formulas leave this substantive judgment to supplied facts.",
    "Offering does not require completed payment or receipt. However, node.bc55be7e973a689d07f9e64b's broader assertions about funding, fulfilment and attribution are not fully established for every third-party arrangement by the supplied circular.",
    "Missing external gift authorities are Code of Conduct paragraph 3.11 and the answer to question 1 of the SFC FAQs issued on 30 September 2010. Can their applicable versions be supplied to verify definitions and qualifications beyond the circular's express rule? No dependency IDs are supplied.",
    "Independent verification of the broader advertising regime requires Code of Conduct paragraph 2.3, the Advertising Guidelines Applicable to Collective Investment Schemes Authorized under the Product Codes, and applicable FAQs and supplementary guidance referenced by footnote 4. Can those versions be supplied? The express advertising claims assessed here need no additional dependency for source support.",
    "The advertising claims retain the services described in paragraph 3 and the marketing context in paragraphs 15–16. They do not prohibit every reference to positive or guaranteed returns, or regulate every service without qualification.",
    "No concrete applicability interval is supplied. The candidates' temporal-basis wording does not establish the applicable date or versions of external authorities.",
    "Satisfaction of the selected gift control, or absence of a caught gift component, does not establish overall permission or compliance with structured-product, advertising, disclosure or redemption requirements."
  ],
